### Bug Description

when using `Modules.Documents.Params.Filters.ObjectNotation` in custom funcitons like:
```ts
function filterEntries<const TSchemaUID extends UID.ContentType>({name, params: {filters, populate}}: {
    name: TSchemaUID,
    params: {
        filters?: Modules.Documents.Params.Filters.ObjectNotation<TSchemaUID>,
        populate?: Modules.Documents.Params.Populate.Any<TSchemaUID>,
    },
}) {
    return strapi.documents(name).findMany({
        filters,
        populate,
    });
}
```

ObjectNotation causes error "TS2589: Type instantiation is excessively deep and possibly infinite." or at the very least significant TypeScript inference delay, due to the recursive type definition causing performance issues in the TypeScript compiler

### Steps to Reproduce

use the `Modules.Documents.Params.Filters.ObjectNotation` type in any function like the one in `Bug Description`
example of an usage of `filterEntries`:
```ts
filterEntries({
    name: 'api::article.article',
    params: {
        filters: {
            $or: [
                {
                    slug: {
                        $notNull: true,
                    },
                },
            ],
        },
    },
});
```

### Expected Behavior

Instant type inference with proper type information (when available, of course)

