### Bug Description

the following response (see `Steps to Reproduce`) occurs when "__component" key in a DZ is presided by a Component (inside the DZ component), or a Relation;
I've traced the issue to the `traverseEntity` function from the "@strapi/utils" package

### Steps to Reproduce

from a fresh install:
- `pnpm dlx create-strapi-app@latest` (v5.52.2 at the time)
    - no login, yes to all
- `pnpm run develop`
- create an admin account
- change the default `shared.quote` component as follows:
    - add another field named "authorImage" that is a singe (existing) component named "shared.media" (it has a media field)
- save the changes (wait for the server to restart)
- in the articles collection, change "shared.quote" component in blocks to have an authorImage (pick any image as file, it's irrelevant)
- save the changes as draft
- copy the &lt;documentId&gt; from the url and make a GET request to "//localhost:1337/api/articles/<documentId\>?status=draft&populate[blocks][on][shared.quote][populate]=*"
- copy the entire response and make a PUT request to the same url:
    - but remove the following keys: "meta, data.id, data.documentId, data.createdAt, data.updatedAt, data.blocks[0].id" (keep "data.blocks[0].authorImage.id")
    - also use a Bearer Authentication token that has permissions, like the Full Access token created by default
    - note that the error might not appear if "data.blocks[0].__component" is before "data.blocks[0].authorImage"
- you should get the following response/error:
```json
{
    "data": null,
    "error": {
        "status": 400,
        "name": "ValidationError",
        "message": "Invalid key __component at blocks",
        "details": {
            "key": "__component",
            "path": "blocks",
            "source": "body"
        }
    }
}
```

### Expected Behavior

the request to pass with status 200, the data to be saved in the DB and the proper response to be returned (like with the GET request)

