### Bug Description

The `@strapi/upgrade` tool fails with `Failed to parse URL from undefined/@strapi/strapi` when upgrading Strapi v4 projects that use Yarn v1 (Classic). The tool incorrectly attempts to use the Yarn v2+ (Berry) registry command, which doesn't exist in Yarn v1, causing registry detection to fail.

> npx @strapi/upgrade major --dry --debug
[WARN]	[2026-03-26T11:44:08.717Z] Please make sure you've created a backup of your codebase and files before upgrading
[DEBUG]	[2026-03-26T11:44:08.926Z] Project: TYPE=application; CWD=/Users/emanuel/Documents/GitHub/gm-cloud-strapi/app; PATHS=./{src,config,public}/**/*.{js,mjs,ts,jsx,tsx,json},!./**/node_modules/**/*,!./**/dist/**/*,package.json
[DEBUG]	[2026-03-26T11:44:08.926Z] Application: VERSION=v0.15.1; STRAPI_VERSION=v4.26.1
[DEBUG]	[2026-03-26T11:44:09.090Z] Using package manager registry: undefined
[ERROR]	[2026-03-26T11:44:09.096Z] Failed to parse URL from undefined/@strapi/strapi

### Steps to Reproduce

1. Create or use an existing Strapi v4.26.1 project with Yarn v1 (only `yarn.lock`, no `package-lock.json`)
2. Verify Yarn registry is configured:

   ```bash
   yarn config get registry
   # Should return: https://registry.npmjs.org/
3. Attempt to upgrade:

    `npx @strapi/upgrade@latest major --dry --debug`
4. Observe the error: Using package manager registry: undefined

### Expected Behavior

The upgrade tool should:
1. Detect that the project uses Yarn v1
2. Successfully retrieve the registry URL using `yarn config get registry`
3. Proceed with the upgrade process using the detected registry
4. Apply codemods and update dependencies as intended

### Logs

```shell
> npx @strapi/upgrade major --dry --debug
[WARN]	[2026-03-26T11:44:08.717Z] Please make sure you've created a backup of your codebase and files before upgrading
[DEBUG]	[2026-03-26T11:44:08.926Z] Project: TYPE=application; CWD=/Users/emanuel/Documents/GitHub/gm-cloud-strapi/app; PATHS=./{src,config,public}/**/*.{js,mjs,ts,jsx,tsx,json},!./**/node_modules/**/*,!./**/dist/**/*,package.json
[DEBUG]	[2026-03-26T11:44:08.926Z] Application: VERSION=v0.15.1; STRAPI_VERSION=v4.26.1
[DEBUG]	[2026-03-26T11:44:09.090Z] Using package manager registry: undefined
[ERROR]	[2026-03-26T11:44:09.096Z] Failed to parse URL from undefined/@strapi/strapi
```

### Code Snippets

**Buggy code location:**
`packages/utils/upgrade/src/modules/npm/package.ts` (lines 72-75)

```typescript
const registryCommands = {
yarn: ['config', 'get', 'npmRegistryServer'],  // Yarn v2+ only
npm: ['config', 'get', 'registry'],
} as const;

```
Issue: The command yarn config get npmRegistryServer only works in Yarn v2+ (Berry). Yarn v1 uses yarn config get registry.

#### Verification:
`yarn config get npmRegistryServer ` Returns: `undefined` 
`yarn config get registry` Returns: `https://registry.yarnpkg.com` 

